 v=d.sort_values('edge_total_variation');axes[1].barh(v.team,v.edge_total_variation,color=np.where(v.regression_eligible,'#287b9b','#b9b9b9'));axes[1].set_xlabel('Passing-link share distance (total variation)');axes[1].set_title('Deleted baseline versus actual missed games\nGrey: excluded from primary fit');fig.suptitle('How closely does deleting the star reproduce the actual network?',fontsize=16);fig.tight_layout(rect=[0,.04,1,.94]);fig.savefig(out/'prediction_actual_comparison.pdf');fig.savefig(out/'prediction_actual_comparison.png',dpi=160);plt.close(fig)
 text=['# Deleted-star baseline versus actual missed-game networks','All 30 teams use the prior-season on/off-selected player from the original onoff_dependency study. The star is the largest qualifying 2024–25 ON minus OFF team offensive-rating gap among players retained in the first ten follow-up games (≥1,000 prior ON minutes and ≥500 OFF minutes). Existing trade-censored windows are unchanged.','## Graph definitions','Original = pooled passing from full games the selected player played. Deleted = zero that player’s row and column in the exact same matrix, without inventing replacement passes. Actual = independently observed passing from full games they missed. This is not an exact on/off-court-stint comparison.','Node AREA is 16,000 times that graph’s involvement share: (passes sent + received)/(2 × team passes). Thus each graph sizes its own nodes and all panels share an area scale. Isolates have zero size and are omitted. Node locations stay fixed. Widths use passes per 1,000 context passes on a shared within-team scale. Normalizing the deleted graph redistributes relative shares only by removing incident passes; it is not a behavioral forecast.','## Comparison measures','Entropy is outgoing conditional H(receiver|passer), weighted by outgoing passes, divided by the same log2(N_union_active−1) within team. Predicted change = H(deleted)−H(original); actual change = H(actual)−H(original). Error = actual−deleted entropy. The error identity is algebraic, not a causal decomposition.','Edge total variation = half the absolute difference of normalized directed edge shares. Zero means identical pass-share allocations; one means disjoint edge support. A value of .30 is 30% of normalized pass-share mass, not 30% of actual passes causally redirected. Node total variation applies the same distance to involvement shares. Jensen–Shannon divergence of joint edge distributions is also exported (bits, 0–1).','Common-donor JS compares each surviving common sender’s conditional recipient distribution. Weights average sender shares in both contexts and renormalize across common senders. Context-only donor mass is exported separately. Recipient changes still include roster availability differences; this is not a fixed-lineup tactical effect.','A separate 500-draw equal-pass-count sensitivity samples original, deleted and actual networks to min(total deleted passes,total actual passes), allowing matched predicted/actual changes and direction agreement. It also compares deleted and actual entropy. Sampling ranges reflect subsampling noise only, not behavioral confidence intervals.','## Qualified versus all-team results',f'{len(primary)} teams meet ≥15 played and ≥10 missed games. Only these enter the prediction-versus-actual change regression. The six small-sample teams are still illustrated but never enter the fitted line. All-30 summaries are descriptive only.','Regression of actual on predicted entropy CHANGE uses OLS/HC3 and conventional Pearson p. Shared original entropy enters both changes, creating possible mathematical coupling; r alone cannot validate prediction. Accuracy is also assessed by direction agreement, mean absolute error and edge/role distances.','|Sample|n|Correct raw direction|Correct equal-count direction|Entropy MAE|Median edge TV|Median role TV|Same main passing hub|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for z in summary:text.append(f"|{z['sample']}|{z['n']}|{z['direction_agreement']}/{z['n']}|{z['equal_count_direction_agreement']}/{z['n']}|{z['entropy_mae']:.4f}|{z['median_edge_tv']:.3f}|{z['median_node_tv']:.3f}|{z['same_main_hub']}/{z['n']}|")
 text+=['## Limits','The original played network pools all played games, including games after some absences. This is a retrospective baseline, not a prospective forecast. The deleted baseline uses no actual absence outcomes to choose replacement edges, but it is not a fitted or validated forecasting model. Large differences can reflect minutes, trades, replacements, other injuries and opponents. A constant unchanged-partner pass allocation is intentionally a simple baseline. Similar entropy can conceal very different links. Current pooled game contexts are unmatched and no causal claim is made. Selection is based on prior-year on/off, not EC or passing volume. Higher entropy is variety, not offensive quality.']
 (out/'METHOD_AND_RESULTS.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(text));print(pd.DataFrame(summary).to_string(index=False));print(stats);return 0
